{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.dht\n     2\t  \"The linker over `dao.jing.dht`, as plain Clojure (docs/design/\n     3\t   yin.vm.linker.dht.md sections 4, 5.4, 7 and 10; slice L2): publish a\n     4\t   module through a `dao.space.dht` node, load its closure onto another\n     5\t   node by manifest address, check its dependency names against the\n     6\t   reader's own name environment, and link it over the node's local store.\n     7\t\n     8\t   The load is `dao.space.dht/load` with the closure walker of\n     9\t   `yin.vm.linker.closure` as its walk: the node stays the only step\n    10\t   owner and fetches each blob the walk answers missing.  A link runs\n    11\t   only after the whole closure is `:loaded`, over a local runtime on the\n    12\t   node's own store, so it asks no peer for anything.\n    13\t\n    14\t   Names come from the reader's composition: the principals it declares\n    15\t   and the index snapshots it chose to load.  Nothing here is read from an\n    16\t   index as authority, and nothing depends on `yin.repl`.\"\n    17\t  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    18\t            [clojure.string :as str]\n    19\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    20\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    21\t            [dao.space.store :as durable]\n    22\t            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]\n    23\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]\n    24\t            [yin.vm.linker.authority :as authority]\n    25\t            [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\n    26\t            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    27\t            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\t(def module-kind\n    31\t  \"The `:kind` of a module closure load.\"\n    32\t  :yin.module/manifest)\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- refused\n    36\t  [reason data]\n    37\t  (merge {:status :refused :reason reason} data))\n    38\t\n    39\t\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t;; Publication (5.4)\n    42\t;; =============================================================================\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn publish!\n    45\t  \"`publish-module!` on the node's store: the blobs join the node's\n    46\t   current publication window, reported by the announcement that closes\n    47\t   it.\"\n    48\t  [node spec]\n    49\t  (publish/publish-module! (dht/store node) spec))\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\t(defn publish-name!\n    53\t  \"Publish the module `name` exporting `exports`, derived from the\n    54\t   publisher's own index `db` (`module-from-index`, section 5.3), through\n    55\t   the node's store, and sign what binds the name to it (6.6): answers\n    56\t   `{:status :ok :address a :links {...} :envelopes [...]}`, each envelope\n    57\t   `publish/assertion`'s answer, for the caller to enter into its index\n    58\t   as one transaction (6.1) before it announces.  Without `key` it is\n    59\t   refused `:yin.link.publish/no-key`; any refusal writes nothing.\n    60\t   `opts` also carries `module-from-index`'s `:primitives`, `:modules`\n    61\t   and `:host-modules`.\"\n    62\t  [node db {:keys [key name] :as opts}]\n    63\t  (if-not key\n    64\t    (refused :yin.link.publish/no-key {:name name})\n    65\t    (let [spec (publish/module-from-index db opts)\n    66\t          res (if (= :refused (:status spec)) spec (publish! node spec))]\n    67\t      (if (= :refused (:status res))\n    68\t        res\n    69\t        (assoc (select-keys res [:address :links])\n    70\t               :status :ok\n    71\t               :envelopes (publish/name-envelopes db key name (:address res)))))))\n    72\t\n    73\t\n    74\t;; =============================================================================\n    75\t;; The module load (4.3)\n    76\t;; =============================================================================\n    77\t\n    78\t(defn closure-walk\n    79\t  \"The closure walk of `manifest-address` as a `dao.space.dht` load walk:\n    80\t   the walker's three outcomes in the load's three shapes.\"\n    81\t  [manifest-address]\n    82\t  (fn [handle]\n    83\t    (let [w (closure/walk handle manifest-address)]\n    84\t      (case (:yin.link.closure/outcome w)\n    85\t        :missing {::dht/walk :missing :address (:address w)}\n    86\t        :complete {::dht/walk :complete :value w}\n    87\t        :invalid {::dht/walk :invalid :address (:address w) :defect (:defect w)}))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn load-module\n    91\t  \"Start loading the closure of `manifest-address` onto `node`; answers\n    92\t   the node.  `dao.space.dht/step` fetches what is missing.\"\n    93\t  [node manifest-address]\n    94\t  (dht/load node manifest-address {:kind module-kind\n    95\t                                   :walk (closure-walk manifest-address)}))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn module-status\n    99\t  \"The load status of `manifest-address` (4.3), or nil.\"\n   100\t  [node manifest-address]\n   101\t  (dht/load-status node manifest-address))\n   102\t\n   103\t\n   104\t(defn load-refusal\n   105\t  \"The section 9 response row of a failed closure load: `status` as\n   106\t   `module-status` answers it.  `:miss` is `:absent` with the miss\n   107\t   `:cause`, `:invalid` is `:descriptor-defect` with the defect's `:code`\n   108\t   (and its `:detail` and `:text` when present), and `:unaskable` is\n   109\t   `:yin.link.dht/unaskable` with the client's `:outcome`.  nil for a load\n   110\t   that has not failed.  The DHT link source refuses with it.\"\n   111\t  [status]\n   112\t  (when (= :failed (:status status))\n   113\t    (let [{::dht/keys [failure] :keys [address cause defect outcome]} (:reason status)]\n   114\t      (case failure\n   115\t        :miss (refused :absent {:address address :cause cause})\n   116\t        :invalid (refused :descriptor-defect\n   117\t                          (merge {:address address :code (:code defect)}\n   118\t                                 (select-keys defect [:detail :text])))\n   119\t        :unaskable (refused :yin.link.dht/unaskable\n   120\t                            {:address address :outcome outcome})))))\n   121\t\n   122\t\n   123\t(defn- not-loaded\n   124\t  [node manifest-address]\n   125\t  (refused :yin.link.dht/not-loaded\n   126\t           {:address manifest-address\n   127\t            :load (dissoc (module-status node manifest-address) :value)}))\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- loaded-closure\n   131\t  [node manifest-address]\n   132\t  (let [status (module-status node manifest-address)]\n   133\t    (when (and (= :loaded (:status status)) (= module-kind (:kind status)))\n   134\t      (:value status))))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t;; =============================================================================\n   138\t;; Names: the snapshot set and the fold (7.2, 7.3)\n   139\t;; =============================================================================\n   140\t\n   141\t(defn head\n   142\t  \"The manifest the HEAD of the node's directory names, or nil: a node\n   143\t   over a durable directory store (`dao.space.store`) has one once its\n   144\t   publisher has written it; any other node has none.\"\n   145\t  [node]\n   146\t  (when-some [dir (:durable-dir (dht/local node))]\n   147\t    (some-> (fs/read-file-text dir durable/head-name)\n   148\t            str/trim\n   149\t            edn/read-string\n   150\t            :manifest)))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn snapshots\n   154\t  \"The node's snapshot set (7.2) as the sorted vector of its addresses:\n   155\t   the manifest its directory's HEAD names, when there is one, and every\n   156\t   index manifest whose load is `:loaded`.  Nothing else in the local\n   157\t   store is considered.\"\n   158\t  [node]\n   159\t  (vec (sort-by str (distinct (cond-> (vec (dht/loaded-indexes node))\n   160\t                                (head node) (conj (head node)))))))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- snapshot-datoms\n   164\t  \"The datoms of the snapshot `s`: a loaded index's, or HEAD's read from\n   165\t   the node's own store.\"\n   166\t  [node s]\n   167\t  (or (dht/loaded-datoms node s)\n   168\t      (index/read-datoms (dht/local node) s)))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn- snapshot-events\n   172\t  \"The authority events of every snapshot, assembled per snapshot (an\n   173\t   entity id is local to its index) and concatenated in snapshot order,\n   174\t   each envelope with its proof once.\"\n   175\t  [node snapshot]\n   176\t  (into []\n   177\t        (comp (mapcat (fn [s]\n   178\t                        (authority/events-from-datoms\n   179\t                          (filter (fn [[_ a]]\n   180\t                                    (contains? #{:yin.module/envelope\n   181\t                                                 :yin.module/proof}\n   182\t                                               a))\n   183\t                                  (snapshot-datoms node s)))))\n   184\t              (distinct))\n   185\t        snapshot))\n   186\t\n   187\t\n   188\t(defn authority\n   189\t  \"The reader's authority from its composition (7.1): each declared\n   190\t   public key (64 lowercase hex) a principal whose proof is an Ed25519\n   191\t   signature (6.3), at `:seq-floor` 0, and `name-env`'s direct entries.\"\n   192\t  [{:keys [principals name-env]}]\n   193\t  {:principals (into {}\n   194\t                     (map (fn [public]\n   195\t                            [(sign/principal public)\n   196\t                             {:proof :yin.module/signature\n   197\t                              :key public\n   198\t                              :verify sign/verify-envelope\n   199\t                              :seq-floor 0}]))\n   200\t                     principals)\n   201\t   :name-env (or name-env {})})\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t(defn- fold\n   205\t  \"The fold of the reader's snapshot set under `authority`\n   206\t   `{:principals {principal declaration} :name-env {name address}}`, and\n   207\t   every envelope it saw by id.  A retraction whose target is not an\n   208\t   assertion the snapshot set holds -- none, or another retraction --\n   209\t   names no name, so its diagnostic moves from `:diagnostics` to\n   210\t   `:global-diagnostics`, once (owner decision 6).\"\n   211\t  [node authority]\n   212\t  (let [snapshot (snapshots node)\n   213\t        events (snapshot-events node snapshot)\n   214\t        env (authority/name-environment\n   215\t              {:snapshot snapshot :principals (or (:principals authority) {})}\n   216\t              events)\n   217\t        envelopes (into {}\n   218\t                        (map (fn [e]\n   219\t                               (let [env (:yin.module/envelope e)]\n   220\t                                 [(authority/assertion-id env) env])))\n   221\t                        events)\n   222\t        ;; global unless the target is an assertion in the set: only an\n   223\t        ;; assertion carries a name\n   224\t        global? (fn [d]\n   225\t                  (and (= :dangling-retraction (:reason d))\n   226\t                       (not= :assert (:yin.module/op (get envelopes (:of d))))))]\n   227\t    {:env (-> env\n   228\t              (assoc :diagnostics (filterv (complement global?) (:diagnostics env))\n   229\t                     :global-diagnostics (filterv global? (:diagnostics env)))\n   230\t              (update :names into\n   231\t                      (map (fn [[n address]]\n   232\t                             [n {:status :ok :address address\n   233\t                                 :yin.link/provenance :composition}]))\n   234\t                      (:name-env authority)))\n   235\t     :envelopes envelopes}))\n   236\t\n   237\t\n   238\t(defn names\n   239\t  \"The reader's name environment: `authority/name-environment` over the\n   240\t   envelopes of the loaded index snapshots, under the principals\n   241\t   `authority` declares, with its direct `:name-env` entries winning,\n   242\t   their provenance `:composition`.  A retraction whose target is not an\n   243\t   assertion in the snapshot set (an assertion outside it, or a\n   244\t   retraction) is under `:global-diagnostics`, once, with\n   245\t   its `:principal` and the assertion id it names under `:of`; it is in\n   246\t   no per-name diagnostic.\"\n   247\t  [node authority]\n   248\t  (:env (fold node authority)))\n   249\t\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- diagnostics-for\n   252\t  \"The fold's diagnostics whose envelope binds or retracts `n`.\"\n   253\t  [{:keys [env envelopes]} n]\n   254\t  (let [name-of (fn [e]\n   255\t                  (if (= :retract (:yin.module/op e))\n   256\t                    (:yin.module/name (get envelopes (:yin.module/of e)))\n   257\t                    (:yin.module/name e)))]\n   258\t    (filterv (fn [d] (= n (name-of (get envelopes (:id d)))))\n   259\t             (:diagnostics env))))\n   260\t\n   261\t\n   262\t(defn resolve-name\n   263\t  \"The name `n` in the reader's name environment: its `names` entry when\n   264\t   it resolves, else its section 9 refusal -- `:absent` with the fold's\n   265\t   `:diagnostics` for that name, or `:ambiguous-name` with every\n   266\t   `:addresses` and `:asserters`.\"\n   267\t  [node authority n]\n   268\t  (let [folded (fold node authority)\n   269\t        entry (get-in folded [:env :names n])]\n   270\t    (cond\n   271\t      (= :ok (:status entry)) entry\n   272\t\n   273\t      (= :ambiguous-name (:reason entry))\n   274\t      (refused :ambiguous-name (merge {:name n}\n   275\t                                      (select-keys entry [:addresses :asserters])))\n   276\t\n   277\t      :else\n   278\t      (refused :absent {:name n :diagnostics (diagnostics-for folded n)}))))\n   279\t\n   280\t\n   281\t;; =============================================================================\n   282\t;; Dependency bindings (7.4)\n   283\t;; =============================================================================\n   284\t\n   285\t\n   286\t(defn dependency-bindings\n   287\t  \"One entry per requirement of the loaded closure of `manifest-address`,\n   288\t   in walk order: whether the dependency's name resolves, in the reader's\n   289\t   own name environment, to the address its publisher pinned.  `:binding`\n   290\t   is `:ok`, `:absent` (with the fold's `:diagnostics` for that name),\n   291\t   `:ambiguous` (`:addresses`, `:asserters`) or `:mismatch` (`:resolved`,\n   292\t   `:asserters`).  Refused `:yin.link.dht/not-loaded` unless the closure\n   293\t   is `:loaded`.\"\n   294\t  [node authority manifest-address]\n   295\t  (if-some [w (loaded-closure node manifest-address)]\n   296\t    (let [folded (fold node authority)]\n   297\t      (mapv (fn [{:keys [module name manifest]}]\n   298\t              (let [entry (get-in folded [:env :names name])\n   299\t                    base {:module module :name name :pinned manifest}\n   300\t                    asserters (get-in entry [:yin.link/provenance\n   301\t                                             :yin.module/asserted-by])]\n   302\t                (cond\n   303\t                  (= :ambiguous-name (:reason entry))\n   304\t                  (assoc base :binding :ambiguous\n   305\t                         :addresses (:addresses entry)\n   306\t                         :asserters (:asserters entry))\n   307\t\n   308\t                  (not= :ok (:status entry))\n   309\t                  (assoc base :binding :absent\n   310\t                         :diagnostics (diagnostics-for folded name))\n   311\t\n   312\t                  (= manifest (:address entry))\n   313\t                  (assoc base :binding :ok)\n   314\t\n   315\t                  :else\n   316\t                  (assoc base :binding :mismatch\n   317\t                         :resolved (:address entry)\n   318\t                         :asserters (or asserters [:composition])))))\n   319\t            (:requires w)))\n   320\t    (not-loaded node manifest-address)))\n   321\t\n   322\t\n   323\t;; =============================================================================\n   324\t;; Link (4.1 step 4)\n   325\t;; =============================================================================\n   326\t\n   327\t(defn link\n   328\t  \"`link-manifest` of `format-kw` through `manifest-address` over the\n   329\t   node's local store, `:verifying` with discharge deferred unless `opts`\n   330\t   says otherwise.  Refused `:yin.link.dht/not-loaded` unless the closure\n   331\t   is `:loaded`; a link refused `:absent` after it is a walker defect,\n   332\t   `:yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete`.\"\n   333\t  ([node manifest-address format-kw]\n   334\t   (link node manifest-address format-kw nil))\n   335\t  ([node manifest-address format-kw opts]\n   336\t   (let [format (some #(when (= format-kw (:format %)) %) publish/code-formats)]\n   337\t     (cond\n   338\t       (nil? (loaded-closure node manifest-address))\n   339\t       (not-loaded node manifest-address)\n   340\t\n   341\t       (nil? format)\n   342\t       (linker/refused :unsupported-format {:format format-kw})\n   343\t\n   344\t       :else\n   345\t       (let [res (publish/link-local (dht/local node) manifest-address format opts)]\n   346\t         (if (= :absent (:reason res))\n   347\t           (refused :yin.link.dht/closure-incomplete {:address (:address res)})\n   348\t           res))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
