{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1250,1510p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '700,810p'; rg -n 'pending|resume|publish|names|principal|tree|load-index' test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"  1250\t  [state]\n  1251\t  (let [{:keys [observer consumer]}\n  1252\t        (macro/step {:observer (:observer state), :consumer (:expander state)})\n  1253\t        [expander summary] (macro/drain-errors consumer)]\n  1254\t    [(assoc state :observer observer :expander expander) summary]))\n  1255\t\n  1256\t\n  1257\t(defn- run-evaluator-stage\n  1258\t  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n  1259\t   expanded tree packet into the VM, runs it, and answers its value on the\n  1260\t   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n  1261\t   the other.\"\n  1262\t  [{:keys [load-program output-stream] :as state}]\n  1263\t  (let [{:keys [observer] vm :consumer}\n  1264\t        (observer/run-on-stream {:observer (:row-observer state),\n  1265\t                                 :consumer (:vm state)}\n  1266\t                                engine/ready-for-ingress?\n  1267\t                                load-program\n  1268\t                                (make-runner output-stream (round-id state)))]\n  1269\t    (assoc state :row-observer observer :vm vm)))\n  1270\t\n  1271\t\n  1272\t(defn- format-expansion-errors\n  1273\t  [errors]\n  1274\t  (str/join \"\\n\" (map #(str \"Error: Macro expansion failed: \" (format-value %))\n  1275\t                      errors)))\n  1276\t\n  1277\t\n  1278\t(defn- link-waiting?\n  1279\t  \"True while `vm` parks on a link wait: the two link states `require`\n  1280\t   parks in, or the install it waits on (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.2).\n  1281\t   These are the reasons the shell's interpreter can move, so they are\n  1282\t   the ones a round drives before reporting the VM wedged.\"\n  1283\t  [vm]\n  1284\t  (boolean (some #(contains? #{:link-request :link-response :install}\n  1285\t                             (:reason %))\n  1286\t                 (:wait-set vm))))\n  1287\t\n  1288\t\n  1289\t(defn- carry-link-identity\n  1290\t  \"The round's base VM with the link identity `used` has already minted\n  1291\t   carried forward: link ids `[origin counter]` and install-child origin\n  1292\t   tags are minted once and never reused on a pair (yin.vm.linker.md\n  1293\t   section 7.2), and the shell's rollback to the round's base -- whose\n  1294\t   counters never advanced -- must not let a later require or install\n  1295\t   mint an identity the pair has already answered.\"\n  1296\t  [base used]\n  1297\t  (let [n (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) (or (:id-counter used) 0))\n  1298\t        o (max (or (:origins base) 0) (or (:origins used) 0))]\n  1299\t    (cond-> base\n  1300\t      (pos? n) (assoc :id-counter n)\n  1301\t      (pos? o) (assoc :origins o))))\n  1302\t\n  1303\t\n  1304\t(defn- link-raise\n  1305\t  \"The raise of a resumed link wait, carrying the identity the parked\n  1306\t   evaluation has minted so far -- the counters of the VM the raise\n  1307\t   interrupted, whose every earlier run is in them -- so a rollback\n  1308\t   cannot reuse it.  It carries the query interpreter's pair too: the\n  1309\t   requests it has answered stay answered when the shell rolls back.\"\n  1310\t  [error vm state]\n  1311\t  (ex-info (or (ex-message error) \"Link failed\")\n  1312\t           (assoc (or (ex-data error) {})\n  1313\t                  ::link-counter (:id-counter vm)\n  1314\t                  ::link-origins (:origins vm)\n  1315\t                  ::query-pair (:query-pair state)\n  1316\t                  ::link-pair (:link-pair state)\n  1317\t                  ::dht (:dht state)\n  1318\t                  ::indexer (:indexer state))))\n  1319\t\n  1320\t\n  1321\t(defn- carry-served\n  1322\t  \"`state` rolled back by a link raise, keeping what the interpreters\n  1323\t   already concluded: the query pair, the link pair past every request\n  1324\t   answered, the DHT node a load started or forgot on, and the indexer\n  1325\t   a `yin.link/publish` committed its name envelopes through.\"\n  1326\t  [state d]\n  1327\t  (cond-> state\n  1328\t    (::query-pair d) (assoc :query-pair (::query-pair d))\n  1329\t    (::link-pair d) (assoc :link-pair (::link-pair d))\n  1330\t    (contains? d ::dht) (assoc :dht (::dht d))\n  1331\t    (::indexer d) (assoc :indexer (::indexer d))))\n  1332\t\n  1333\t\n  1334\t(defn- link-context\n  1335\t  \"What a `yin.link` call is answered under (yin.repl.query/serve): the\n  1336\t   reader's authority, the publisher's key, and the requesting VM's\n  1337\t   primitives and module registry -- the modules it linked are derived\n  1338\t   from it, never recorded -- and the round.\"\n  1339\t  [state vm]\n  1340\t  {:authority (link/authority (:link-source state))\n  1341\t   :key (:dht-key state)\n  1342\t   :primitives (:primitives vm)\n  1343\t   :modules (:modules vm)\n  1344\t   :round (:round state)})\n  1345\t\n  1346\t\n  1347\t(defn- drive-links\n  1348\t  \"Serve the linker interpreter and run the parked VM alternately, at most\n  1349\t   `link-round-budget` rounds, while `vm` waits on a link.  A round that\n  1350\t   moves nothing ends the drive: a link whose content source cannot\n  1351\t   answer will not answer by waiting longer.  Returns\n  1352\t   `[state vm pending progress?]`, `pending` the links the interpreter\n  1353\t   reported `:pending`, and `progress?` true when a round moved\n  1354\t   something -- advanced a serve cursor, delivered a response or\n  1355\t   completed an install -- the fact the pending run's `:checks` resets\n  1356\t   on (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3.1).  A refused or lost link\n  1357\t   raises as the VM's own, carrying the interrupted VM's minted\n  1358\t   identity.\n  1359\t\n  1360\t   A VM waiting on a `dao.space.query/q` call is driven the same way: the\n  1361\t   query interpreter (`yin.repl.query/serve`) answers from the session's\n  1362\t   indexer and the VM runs on.  Only a round the VM spends waiting on a\n  1363\t   link counts against `link-round-budget`; a query is answered in the\n  1364\t   round it is asked, so its rounds are bounded by `query-drive-budget`\n  1365\t   calls instead: a VM still waiting on a call once the drive has\n  1366\t   answered that many raises `query-call-limit-text` as its own error,\n  1367\t   the unanswered request abandoned with it.\"\n  1368\t  [state vm]\n  1369\t  (loop [i 0\n  1370\t         calls 0\n  1371\t         vm vm\n  1372\t         state state\n  1373\t         pending []\n  1374\t         progress? false]\n  1375\t    (let [link? (link-waiting? vm)\n  1376\t          query? (query/waiting? vm)]\n  1377\t      (cond\n  1378\t        (or (vm/halted? vm) (not (or link? query?)) (>= i link-round-budget))\n  1379\t        [state vm pending progress?]\n  1380\t\n  1381\t        (and query? (>= calls query-drive-budget))\n  1382\t        (throw (link-raise (ex-info query-call-limit-text\n  1383\t                                    {:reason :yin.repl.query/call-limit\n  1384\t                                     :limit query-drive-budget})\n  1385\t                           vm\n  1386\t                           (update state :query-pair query/abandon-requests)))\n  1387\t\n  1388\t        :else\n  1389\t        (let [served (when link?\n  1390\t                       (link/serve {:pair (:link-pair state)\n  1391\t                                    :source (:link-source state)\n  1392\t                                    :dht (:dht state)}))\n  1393\t              state (cond-> state\n  1394\t                      served (assoc :link-pair (:pair served)\n  1395\t                                    :dht (:dht served)))\n  1396\t              answered (when query?\n  1397\t                         (query/serve {:pair (:query-pair state)\n  1398\t                                       :indexer (:indexer state)\n  1399\t                                       :ast-indexer (:ast-indexer state)\n  1400\t                                       :dht (:dht state)\n  1401\t                                       :link (link-context state vm)\n  1402\t                                       :limits {:row-limit query-row-limit\n  1403\t                                                :byte-limit query-byte-limit}\n  1404\t                                       :budget (min query-serve-budget\n  1405\t                                                    (- query-drive-budget\n  1406\t                                                       calls))}))\n  1407\t              state (cond-> state\n  1408\t                      answered (assoc :query-pair (:pair answered)\n  1409\t                                      :dht (:dht answered)\n  1410\t                                      :indexer (:indexer answered)))\n  1411\t              pending (if (seq (:pending served)) (:pending served) pending)]\n  1412\t          (if (or (:progress? served) (:progress? answered))\n  1413\t            (let [vm' (try (vm/run vm)\n  1414\t                           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error)\n  1415\t                                  error\n  1416\t                             (throw (link-raise error vm state))))]\n  1417\t              (recur (if link? (inc i) i)\n  1418\t                     (+ calls (:answered answered 0))\n  1419\t                     vm'\n  1420\t                     state\n  1421\t                     pending\n  1422\t                     true))\n  1423\t            [state vm pending progress?]))))))\n  1424\t\n  1425\t\n  1426\t(defn- tokenize\n  1427\t  \"Answer the halted VM's value on the output medium under `state`'s\n  1428\t   round, as the evaluator runner does for a program it runs itself.  A\n  1429\t   resumed require halts outside the observer loop, so the shell emits\n  1430\t   its token here.\"\n  1431\t  [state vm]\n  1432\t  ((make-runner (:output-stream state) (round-id state)) vm))\n  1433\t\n  1434\t\n  1435\t(defn- pending-text\n  1436\t  [pending]\n  1437\t  (if (seq pending)\n  1438\t    (str \";; require pending: \"\n  1439\t         (str/join \", \" (map (fn [p]\n  1440\t                               (str (pr-str (:name p))\n  1441\t                                    \" (link \" (pr-str (:yin.link/id p)) \")\"))\n  1442\t                             pending))\n  1443\t         \"); lines typed meanwhile run when it completes, (abandon) gives\"\n  1444\t         \" up\\n\")\n  1445\t    (str \";; require still pending; lines typed meanwhile run when it\"\n  1446\t         \" completes, (abandon) gives up\\n\")))\n  1447\t\n  1448\t\n  1449\t(defn- dropped-lines-text\n  1450\t  [n]\n  1451\t  (when (pos? n)\n  1452\t    (str \";; dropped \" n \" line\" (when (> n 1) \"s\")\n  1453\t         \" typed while the require was pending\\n\")))\n  1454\t\n  1455\t\n  1456\t(def ^:private policy-abandon-text\n  1457\t  \"The message a policy-driven abandon prints, in the shape of the\n  1458\t   `(abandon)` notice, so a policy abandon is never mistaken for a\n  1459\t   user's (yin.repl.link-policy.md section 3.3).\"\n  1460\t  \";; the session link policy ended the require\\n\")\n  1461\t\n  1462\t\n  1463\t(defn- abandon-pending\n  1464\t  \"Give up the shell's `:pending-run` (section 7.2, step 7, the abandoned\n  1465\t   case): every install in flight is dropped through the engine's own\n  1466\t   `refused`, every link wait entry is retired with the reason raised as\n  1467\t   the require's error, and the shell returns to the round the require\n  1468\t   began in, whose store and value history the parked evaluation never\n  1469\t   wrote.  Lines typed while the require was pending are dropped with\n  1470\t   it, and said so.  The linker side learns nothing: no response was\n  1471\t   ever promised, and one that still arrives is skipped as late.  The\n  1472\t   identity the parked evaluation minted -- link ids and child origins\n  1473\t   -- is carried onto the base, so nothing is minted twice on the\n  1474\t   surviving pair.  The `(abandon)` command retires with\n  1475\t   `:yin.repl/abandoned` and no message of its own; the session link\n  1476\t   policy retires with the reason it answered and prints\n  1477\t   `policy-abandon-text`, so a policy abandon is never mistaken for a\n  1478\t   user's.\"\n  1479\t  ([state] (abandon-pending state :yin.repl/abandoned nil))\n  1480\t  ([state reason ended-text]\n  1481\t   (if-let [parked (:pending-run state)]\n  1482\t     (let [[state' text] (drain-output state)\n  1483\t           ;; installs first: their waiters leave the wait set with the\n  1484\t           ;; refusal queued, then every remaining link entry retires\n  1485\t           vm (engine/abandon-installs (:vm parked) reason)\n  1486\t           error (try\n  1487\t                   (vm/run (reduce (fn [vm e]\n  1488\t                                     (engine/abandon-link vm (:link-id e)\n  1489\t                                                          reason))\n  1490\t                                   vm\n  1491\t                                   (:wait-set vm)))\n  1492\t                   nil\n  1493\t                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs js/Error) e\n  1494\t                     e))]\n  1495\t       [(assoc state'\n  1496\t               :vm (query/discard-answers\n  1497\t                     (carry-link-identity (:base parked) vm)\n  1498\t                     (:query-pair state'))\n  1499\t               :pending-run nil)\n  1500\t        (str text\n  1501\t             ended-text\n  1502\t             (if error (format-error error) \"\")\n  1503\t             (dropped-lines-text (count (:pending-lines parked))))])\n  1504\t     [state \"Nothing is pending\"])))\n  1505\t\n  1506\t\n  1507\t(defn- consult-link-policy\n  1508\t  \"Consult the shell's `:link-policy` over a run that is still pending --\n  1509\t   when the require parks, and after each re-check that leaves it so;\n  1510\t   never on a re-check that completes it (yin.repl.link-policy.md\n   700\t\n   701\t(defn- dht-op?\n   702\t  [request]\n   703\t  (contains? (set (vals dht-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   704\t\n   705\t\n   706\t(defn- link-op?\n   707\t  [request]\n   708\t  (contains? (set (vals link-ops)) (apply2/request-op request)))\n   709\t\n   710\t\n   711\t(defn- session-modules\n   712\t  \"`[linked hosts]` of the requesting VM's module `registry`: the modules\n   713\t   it linked through the linker, `{name manifest-address}` -- a linked\n   714\t   entry carries its manifest's address -- and the names of its host\n   715\t   modules, which carry none.\"\n   716\t  [registry]\n   717\t  (let [entries (module/module-entries registry)]\n   718\t    [(into {} (keep (fn [[n e]] (when (some? (:address e)) [n (:address e)])))\n   719\t           entries)\n   720\t     (set (keep (fn [[n e]] (when (nil? (:address e)) n)) entries))]))\n   721\t\n   722\t\n   723\t(defn- link-answer\n   724\t  \"The response to one `yin.link` call, from `node` -- the shell's DHT\n   725\t   node -- and `indexer`, the session's code indexer, under the session\n   726\t   composition `ctx` (`:authority`, `:key`, `:primitives`, `:modules`,\n   727\t   `:round`): `names` answers `yin.vm.linker.dht/names`; `publish` answers\n   728\t   `yin.vm.linker.dht/publish-name!` over the published index, whose\n   729\t   name envelopes the indexer then commits and publishes as one\n   730\t   transaction, the HEAD write announcing the round's publication.  A\n   731\t   refusal is answered under its own reason.  Answers `[node indexer\n   732\t   response]`.\"\n   733\t  [node indexer ctx request]\n   734\t  (let [id (apply2/request-id request)\n   735\t        args (apply2/request-args request)\n   736\t        [indexer answer]\n   737\t        (cond\n   738\t          (nil? node)\n   739\t          [indexer (unavailable (str \"the shell has no DHT node; start it with \"\n   740\t                                     \"--index-store dht:<dir>\"))]\n   741\t\n   742\t          (nil? (encoded-size args))\n   743\t          [indexer (invalid \"yin.link takes portable Yin data only\")]\n   744\t\n   745\t          (= ::link-names (apply2/request-op request))\n   746\t          [indexer {:ok (linker.dht/names node (:authority ctx))}]\n   747\t\n   748\t          :else\n   749\t          (let [[name exports] args\n   750\t                db (when (and (symbol? name) (sequential? exports)\n   751\t                              (every? symbol? exports))\n   752\t                     (snapshot indexer))]\n   753\t            (cond\n   754\t              (nil? db)\n   755\t              [indexer (invalid (str \"yin.link/publish expects a module name \"\n   756\t                                     \"and a vector of export names, got \"\n   757\t                                     (pr-str args)))]\n   758\t\n   759\t              (refused? db) [indexer db]\n   760\t\n   761\t              :else\n   762\t              (let [[linked hosts] (session-modules (:modules ctx))\n   763\t                    res (linker.dht/publish-name!\n   764\t                          node db {:name name\n   765\t                                   :exports (vec exports)\n   766\t                                   :key (:key ctx)\n   767\t                                   :primitives (:primitives ctx)\n   768\t                                   :modules linked\n   769\t                                   :host-modules hosts})\n   770\t                    indexer' (if (seq (:envelopes res))\n   771\t                               (repl.index/commit-names indexer (:envelopes res)\n   772\t                                                        (:round ctx))\n   773\t                               indexer)]\n   774\t                (cond\n   775\t                  (= :refused (:status res))\n   776\t                  [indexer (refusal (:reason res)\n   777\t                                    (str \"yin.link/publish refused: \"\n   778\t                                         (pr-str (dissoc res :status :reason)))\n   779\t                                    nil)]\n   780\t\n   781\t                  (not= (:failure indexer) (:failure indexer'))\n   782\t                  [indexer' (unavailable \"the name assertion was not indexed\")]\n   783\t\n   784\t                  :else\n   785\t                  [indexer'\n   786\t                   {:ok {:module name\n   787\t                         :address (:address res)\n   788\t                         :links (into {}\n   789\t                                      (map (fn [[f o]]\n   790\t                                             [f (if (= :ok (:status o))\n   791\t                                                  :ok\n   792\t                                                  (:reason o))]))\n   793\t                                      (:links res))}}])))))]\n   794\t    [node indexer (if (refused? answer)\n   795\t                    {apply2/id-key id, apply2/error-key answer}\n   796\t                    (apply2/success-response id (:ok answer)))]))\n   797\t\n   798\t\n   799\t;; =============================================================================\n   800\t;; The interpreter\n   801\t;; =============================================================================\n   802\t\n   803\t(defn serve\n   804\t  \"One serve round of the query interpreter over `pair`: answer every\n   805\t   request its cursor has not consumed, from `indexer` and `ast-indexer`\n   806\t   as they stand now, at most `budget` of them.  A response is appended before the cursor\n   807\t   moves past its request; one the call-out refuses leaves the request to\n   808\t   be re-read.  A value that is not a request envelope is consumed\n   809\t   unanswered: no call made it.  A `dao.space.dht` call is answered from\n   810\t   `dht`, the shell's DHT node, which a `load-index` advances.  A\n7:   A publishing shell holding an Ed25519 key defines a function and a\n8:   module-level value, and publishes `my.lib` (the function) and\n10:   handed the publisher's index manifest (`--dht-manifest`) and its\n11:   principal (`--dht-principal`) requires each module by name, waits\n12:   through pending, and evaluates the export, on each of the four VMs.\n14:   does not declare the principal, and one handed an index whose proof\n31:            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n58:;; A mesh world of shells and plain publishing peers\n63:  (let [c (mesh/join! net port {::jing.dht/publish? true\n80:   `peer-ports`: publishing when `key` is given (`--dht-publish\n82:   declaring `principals` (`--dht-principal`).\"\n83:  [net dir port peer-ports {:keys [key manifest principals]}]\n88:                        :publish? (some? key)\n95:     :principals (vec principals)}))\n151:(defn- published\n153:  (some #(when (and (= k (:who %)) (= :published (::dht/event %))\n175:(def ^:private publisher-lines\n180:   \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.lib) (quote [f]))\"\n181:   \"(yin.link/publish (quote my.store) (quote [g]))\"])\n184:(defn- publish-world\n185:  \"Peers at 2 and 3 and the publisher `:a` at 1, which types\n186:   `publisher-lines` and settles: `[w manifest]`, its HEAD index manifest\n191:        w (reduce (fn [w line] (first (eval-at w :a line))) w publisher-lines)\n193:        w (run-world w 60000 \"the publisher's HEAD was not reported\"\n194:                     #(published % :a m))]\n196:    (is (= :acknowledged (:result (published w :a m)))\n197:        (pr-str (dissoc (published w :a m) :failed)))\n204:  [w k dir port manifest principals]\n207:                              {:manifest manifest :principals principals}))\n221:                     #(nil? (get-in % [:shells k :pending-run])))]\n230:(deftest a-reader-requires-a-published-module-by-name-on-all-four-vms\n234:        principal (sign/principal (:public key))]\n236:      (let [[w m] (publish-world net adir key)\n238:            names (ld/names (get-in w [:shells :b :dht])\n239:                            (ld/authority {:principals [(:public key)]}))]\n240:        (testing \"the reader resolves both names, each signed by the publisher\"\n242:            (is (= [principal] (get-in names [:names n :yin.link/provenance\n244:                (pr-str (get-in names [:names n])))))\n257:                  (is (str/includes? text \"pending\")\n279:(deftest without-the-principal-the-require-is-absent-undeclared\n284:      (let [[w m] (publish-world net adir key)\n291:        (is (= [[:undeclared-principal (sign/principal (:public key))]]\n292:               (mapv (juxt :reason :principal) (:diagnostics body))))\n303:        principal (sign/principal (:public key))\n304:        ;; an assertion signed but never published: no snapshot holds it\n305:        unpublished (:envelope (publish/assertion key {:name 'my.lib\n308:        of (jing/segment-key unpublished)]\n310:      (let [[w _] (publish-world net adir key)\n312:            dangling (let [r (publish/retraction key {:of of :seq 91})]\n313:                       (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n319:                         #(published % :a dangling))\n322:            [w _] (eval-at w :e \"(yin.link/names)\")\n325:        (testing \"(yin.link/names) carries it once, globally, with principal and id\"\n326:          (is (= [[:dangling-retraction principal of]]\n327:                 (mapv (juxt :reason :principal :of) (:global-diagnostics env)))\n345:        principal (sign/principal (:public key))\n346:        unpublished (:envelope (publish/assertion key {:name 'my.lib\n349:        r1 (publish/retraction key {:of (jing/segment-key unpublished) :seq 91})\n352:        r2 (publish/retraction key {:of r1-id :seq 92})]\n354:      (let [[w _] (publish-world net adir key)\n355:            index (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n363:                         #(published % :a index))\n366:            [w _] (eval-at w :e \"(yin.link/names)\")\n369:        (testing \"(yin.link/names): both retractions are global, each once\"\n370:          (is (= #{[:dangling-retraction principal (jing/segment-key unpublished)]\n371:                   [:dangling-retraction principal r1-id]}\n372:                 (set (mapv (juxt :reason :principal :of) (:global-diagnostics env))))\n383:(deftest an-empty-export-list-publishes-the-no-op-module-at-the-prompt\n388:      (let [[w _] (publish-world net adir key)\n389:            [w text] (eval-at w :a \"(yin.link/publish (quote empty.lib) (quote []))\")\n392:            w (run-world w (+ (:now w) 60000) \"the publisher's HEAD was not reported\"\n393:                         #(published % :a m))]\n416:  \"The publisher's HEAD index `m` with every proof replaced by one `key`\n417:   made over another envelope, published and announced through the\n418:   publisher's own node: its name claims, proofs that do not verify.\"\n420:  (dht-test/publish-datoms!\n438:      (let [[w m] (publish-world net adir key)\n441:                         #(published % :a forged))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"The reader command uses `ed25519:...`, but the CLI accepts only the raw 64-character public key. I also found that publication reports can explicitly say “not retrying”; I’m checking that against the section’s blanket retry claim.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc | sed -n '170,278p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/link.cljc | sed -n '1,310p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc | sed -n '199,290p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
