{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc | sed -n '35,145p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc | sed -n '440,495p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc | sed -n '444,478p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | sed -n '1919,1940p'; rg -n 'inbound-bytes|max-inbound-bytes' src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"    35\t   order: `$ast` rows match `[id tag & slots]` at their exact arity, `$occ`\n    36\t   tuples `[root path node]`.  They are the same session-to-date relations\n    37\t   under either view; `:view` selects only the `$` datom view.  They are\n    38\t   read from the AST indexer the shell holds when it serves, and a lost or\n    39\t   failed one refuses such a query while datom-only queries still answer.\n    40\t\n    41\t   Free variables are a query over these two relations: pass\n    42\t   `yin.vm/occurrence-rules`, the portable data rule set, as the opt-in `%`\n    43\t   input.  The shell ships no binding for it; the user defines or pastes\n    44\t   the literal.  The answer is the raw free set, so it includes `yin/def`\n    45\t   where a definition is present (`yin.vm/free-names` removes it).\n    46\t\n    47\t   Answers and refusals are portable data.  Refusals use the FFI error\n    48\t   envelope under a stable code: `::index-unavailable`, `::invalid-input`,\n    49\t   `::result-limit`, or `::query-failed` for a query the engine rejects.\n    50\t   Limits are the caller's: `serve` takes the row and encoded-byte bound\n    51\t   and checks both before it appends a response.\n    52\t\n    53\t   `(require 'dao.space.dht)` and `(require 'yin.link)` activate two more\n    54\t   host modules the same way, answered over the shell's DHT node through\n    55\t   the plain functions of `dao.space.dht` and `yin.vm.linker.dht`\n    56\t   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 10): each answer checks its arguments, makes one\n    57\t   call into the plain API, and responds; a `yin.link/publish` then\n    58\t   commits the envelopes it signed through the session's indexer.\"\n    59\t  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:typed_data\" :refer [Uint8List]]]\n    60\t                :default [])\n    61\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n    62\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    63\t            [dao.space.dht :as dht]\n    64\t            [dao.space.index :as index]\n    65\t            [dao.space.query :as query]\n    66\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    67\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    68\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    69\t            [yin.repl.ast-index :as ast-index]\n    70\t            [yin.repl.index :as repl.index]\n    71\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    72\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n    73\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n    74\t            [yin.vm.linker.dht :as linker.dht]\n    75\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\t(def module-name\n    79\t  \"The module `(require 'dao.space.query)` activates.\"\n    80\t  'dao.space.query)\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(def op\n    84\t  \"The `dao.stream.apply` operation a `q` call requests.\"\n    85\t  ::q)\n    86\t\n    87\t\n    88\t(def dht-module-name\n    89\t  \"The module `(require 'dao.space.dht)` activates: the plain Clojure DHT\n    90\t   path (`dao.space.dht`) as host functions over the shell's own DHT node.\"\n    91\t  'dao.space.dht)\n    92\t\n    93\t\n    94\t(def dht-ops\n    95\t  \"The `dao.stream.apply` operations the `dao.space.dht` module requests:\n    96\t   `load-index`, `load-status` and `q`, each answered by the\n    97\t   `dao.space.dht` function of that name, `retry` and `cancel`,\n    98\t   answered by `retry!` and `cancel!`, and `load-module` and\n    99\t   `module-status`, answered by the `yin.vm.linker.dht` function of that\n   100\t   name (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 10).\"\n   101\t  {'load-index ::dht-load-index\n   102\t   'load-status ::dht-load-status\n   103\t   'q ::dht-q\n   104\t   'retry ::dht-retry\n   105\t   'cancel ::dht-cancel\n   106\t   'load-module ::dht-load-module\n   107\t   'module-status ::dht-module-status})\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(def link-module-name\n   111\t  \"The module `(require 'yin.link)` activates: publishing a module from\n   112\t   the session's indexed code and reading the reader's name environment\n   113\t   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 10), over the shell's own DHT node.\"\n   114\t  'yin.link)\n   115\t\n   116\t\n   117\t(def link-ops\n   118\t  \"The `dao.stream.apply` operations the `yin.link` module requests:\n   119\t   `publish`, answered by `yin.vm.linker.dht/publish-name!`, and `names`,\n   120\t   answered by `yin.vm.linker.dht/names`.\"\n   121\t  {'publish ::link-publish\n   122\t   'names ::link-names})\n   123\t\n   124\t\n   125\t(def views\n   126\t  \"The options map's `:view` values and the `dao.space.query` interpreter\n   127\t   each names.  `:current` is the default.\"\n   128\t  {:current query/current\n   129\t   :history query/history})\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t;; =============================================================================\n   133\t;; The module and its call\n   134\t;; =============================================================================\n   135\t\n   136\t(defn- q\n   137\t  \"The export: a data constructor.  The effect it returns is answered by\n   138\t   `call-handler`, which parks the caller on the call pair.\"\n   139\t  [& args]\n   140\t  (module/make-effect ::call {:args (vec args)}))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(def ^:private exports\n   144\t  {'q q})\n   145\t\n   440\t                        :dht (dht/state composition)\n   441\t                        :traffic-cursor nil)\n   442\t                 [{::event :bound :host host :port port :id (node-id node)}]])\n   443\t\n   444\t              :dao.stream.datagram/bind-failed\n   445\t              (let [reason (str (:dao.stream.datagram/reason v))]\n   446\t                [(assoc node :refusal (str \"the socket could not bind \"\n   447\t                                           (get-in node [:composition\n   448\t                                                         ::dht/bind-host])\n   449\t                                           \": \" reason))\n   450\t                 [{::event :bind-failed :reason reason}]])\n   451\t\n   452\t              (recur (:dao.stream/cursor next)))\n   453\t\n   454\t            :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor next))\n   455\t            [(assoc node :traffic-cursor cursor) []]))))))\n   456\t\n   457\t\n   458\t(defn- read-all\n   459\t  \"Every value on `handle` after `cursor`: `[values cursor' gap?]`.\"\n   460\t  [handle cursor]\n   461\t  (loop [cursor cursor\n   462\t         acc []\n   463\t         gap? false]\n   464\t    (let [next (stream/next handle cursor)]\n   465\t      (case (:dao.stream/outcome next)\n   466\t        :dao.stream/ok (recur (:dao.stream/cursor next)\n   467\t                              (conj acc (:dao.stream/value next))\n   468\t                              gap?)\n   469\t        :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor next) acc true)\n   470\t        [acc cursor gap?]))))\n   471\t\n   472\t\n   473\t;; =============================================================================\n   474\t;; The ledger: entries and the counts a result reads (5.5.1)\n   475\t;; =============================================================================\n   476\t\n   477\t(defn- retryable?\n   478\t  [entry]\n   479\t  (and (= :failed (:state entry)) (contains? retryable (:reason entry))))\n   480\t\n   481\t\n   482\t(defn- tally\n   483\t  [ledger entry sign]\n   484\t  (cond-> ledger\n   485\t    (= :waiting (:state entry)) (update :waiting + sign)\n   486\t    (= :sent (:state entry)) (update :sent + sign)\n   487\t    (retryable? entry) (update :retryable + sign)))\n   488\t\n   489\t\n   490\t(defn- put-entry\n   491\t  \"`ledger` with `address`'s entry replaced by `entry`, its counts kept.\"\n   492\t  [ledger address entry]\n   493\t  (let [old (get-in ledger [:entries address])]\n   494\t    (-> (cond-> ledger\n   495\t          (nil? old) (update :order conj address)\n   444\t(defn step-all\n   445\t  \"One tick of the single step owner: the local shell first, then the served\n   446\t   endpoint — against the same shell value.  A DHT index store's node is stepped\n   447\t   first (yin.repl.dht/step): its lines print before the shell's, a\n   448\t   hydration still outstanding leaves every typed line waiting in the\n   449\t   input medium, and a refused one stops the shell.  A `--port` process\n   450\t   serves one shared shell, as v1's atom made it: the driver evaluates this tick's local\n   451\t   lines first, so a definition typed at the local prompt is already in the\n   452\t   shell the endpoint evaluates remote requests against in the same tick, and\n   453\t   the endpoint's shell — remote definitions included — is threaded back before\n   454\t   the next tick.  A require parked on a closure load the node ended this\n   455\t   tick is re-checked once, before any typed line, with no line of its\n   456\t   own (yin.repl/recheck-on-load-events, yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2): its\n   457\t   text prints after the node's lines.  Returns `[state server lines]`;\n   458\t   the caller only prints.\"\n   459\t  [state server now]\n   460\t  (let [[repl dht-lines events] (repl.dht/step (:repl state) now)\n   461\t        state (assoc state :repl repl)]\n   462\t    (cond\n   463\t      (repl.dht/refusal repl)\n   464\t      [(assoc state :running? false) server dht-lines]\n   465\t\n   466\t      (not (repl.dht/admitting? repl))\n   467\t      [state server dht-lines]\n   468\t\n   469\t      :else\n   470\t      (let [[repl rechecked] (shell/recheck-on-load-events repl events)\n   471\t            dht-lines (cond-> dht-lines\n   472\t                        (seq rechecked) (conj rechecked))\n   473\t            state (assoc state :repl repl)\n   474\t            stepped (driver/repl-step state now)\n   475\t            [entries state'] (driver/take-outbox stepped)\n   476\t            server' (when server\n   477\t                      (serve/step (assoc-in server [:repl] (:repl state'))\n   478\t                                  now))\n  1919\t    (recheck-pending* state nil)\n  1920\t    [state nil]))\n  1921\t\n  1922\t\n  1923\t(defn recheck-on-load-events\n  1924\t  \"The host ticker's re-check of a pending run over a DHT link source\n  1925\t   (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 8.2): `recheck-pending`, once, if and only if\n  1926\t   `events` -- one tick's `dao.space.dht/step` events -- hold a `:loaded`\n  1927\t   or `:load-failed` event for a manifest a pending link waits on.  Any\n  1928\t   other event, and any event while nothing waits on its manifest,\n  1929\t   answers `[state nil]` with `state` itself: no re-check, no `:checks`.\"\n  1930\t  [state events]\n  1931\t  (let [waits (set (keep :manifest (get-in state [:pending-run :links])))]\n  1932\t    (if (some (fn [e]\n  1933\t                (and (contains? #{:loaded :load-failed} (:dao.space.dht/event e))\n  1934\t                     (contains? waits (:manifest e))))\n  1935\t              events)\n  1936\t      (recheck-pending state)\n  1937\t      [state nil])))\n  1938\t\n  1939\t\n  1940\t(defn- resume-pending\n757:                             (<= (+ (:inbound-bytes state) (byte-count bs))\n758:                                 (::max-inbound-bytes state)))\n794:                        (update :inbound-bytes + (byte-count (:bytes m)))\n1277:               (not (and (integer? (::max-inbound-bytes c))\n1278:                         (<= 0 (::max-inbound-bytes c)))))\n1279:      (throw (defect \"socket composition needs a nonnegative max-inbound-bytes\" {})))\n1301:            :inbound-bytes 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-01 15:48:46 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-01 22:48:46 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\nFound five documentation issues:\n\n1. **P1 — The reader command supplies an invalid principal.** [yin.repl.md:195](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:195) uses `--dht-principal ed25519:...`. The parser accepts exactly 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters, without that prefix ([main.cljc:102](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:102)). Even substituting a complete prefixed principal fails startup. Use the raw public-key hex and explain how it differs from the banner’s principal.\n\n2. **P2 — Unacknowledged publications are not always retried.** [yin.repl.md:183](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:183) promises background retries while the node remains open. Publications with no retryable failures terminate ([dao/space/dht.cljc:918](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:918)); older repairs can also be displaced ([dao/space/dht.cljc:964](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:964)). The shell explicitly prints “not retrying” for those outcomes ([repl/dht.cljc:150](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc:150)). Qualify the promise by the reported repair state.\n\n3. **P2 — The blanket refusal rule incorrectly includes key generation.** [yin.repl.md:128](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:128) says all `--dht-*` flags require a DHT store. `--dht-keygen` is deliberately excluded from the gated flag set ([main.cljc:97](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:97)); startup handles it before composing a store ([main.cljc:366](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:366)), returning exit status 0 ([main.cljc:186](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:186)). Document this exception.\n\n4. **P2 — The example never defines its export.** Publishing `[f]` at [yin.repl.md:173](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:173) from the newly started session refuses `:yin.link.publish/undefined-export` ([publish.cljc:343](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:343)). Nothing establishes the later `4201` result. The cited test first defines `(def f (fn [x] (+ x 4200)))` ([dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:175](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc:175)). Add that prerequisite.\n\n5. **P2 — The prompt does not expose all the listed plain APIs.** [yin.repl.md:246](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/yin.repl.md:246) says requiring `dao.space.dht` exposes “the same calls,” following a list including `join`, `names`, `authority`, and `link`. Its actual operations are `load-index`, `load-status`, `q`, `retry`, `cancel`, `load-module`, and `module-status` ([query.cljc:94](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc:94)). `names` belongs to `yin.link` ([query.cljc:117](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc:117)). Enumerate the supported prompt calls.\n\nAll 137 added lines are ASCII and at most 80 columns. Voice is consistent with the surrounding document. No files were edited and no suites were run.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGES"}}
